{title: Leave It There}
{artist: Charles Albert Tindley}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
If the [G]world from you withhold of its [C]silver and its [G]gold,
and you have to get along with [A]meager [D]fare,
just re[G]member, in his word, how he [C]feeds the little [G]bird —
take your [D]burden to the Lord and [G]leave it there.

Chorus
[G]Leave it there, [C]leave it [G]there — take your [A]burden to the Lord and [D]leave it there;
if you [G]trust and never doubt, [C]he will surely bring you [G]out:
take your [D]burden to the Lord and [G]leave it there.
